 <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:27:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: check only the queue being set in the encoder
 S_FMT
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The encoder's VIDIOC_S_FMT returns -EBUSY when either queue streams.
That forbids setting the OUTPUT format while CAPTURE streams, which the
stateful encoder interface allows. The decoder got the same fix earlier
in this series.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_enc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_enc.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_enc.c
index 2c605f8dd..c71536a7d 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_enc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_enc.c
@@ -1485,7 +1485,8 @@ static int vidioc_s_fmt(struct file *file, void *priv, struct v4l2_format *f)
 	ret = vidioc_try_fmt(file, priv, f);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-	if (ctx->vq_src.streaming || ctx->vq_dst.streaming) {
+	if (f->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE ?
+	    ctx->vq_dst.streaming : ctx->vq_src.streaming) {
 		v4l2_err(&dev->v4l2_dev, "%s queue busy\n", __func__);
 		ret = -EBUSY;
 		goto out;
